    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Assistant-Professor_JR101973": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-13\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Pharmacy Administration Job Summary: The Department of Pharmacy Administration at The University of Mississippi School of Pharmacy is seeking an individual for a full time, tenure-track position for the rank of Assistant Professor. Job Description: Assistant Professor of Pharmacy Administration The Department of Pharmacy Administration at The University of Mississippi School of Pharmacy is seeking an individual for a full time, tenure-track position for the rank of Assistant Professor.  A Ph.D. or comparable degree in pharmacy administration, health services research, or related field is required by the time of employment. Experience in or knowledge of the health care system and/or the field of pharmacy is required. Responsibilities for this position include: teaching at the professional and graduate levels, initiation of research projects, and participation in collaborative research projects of mutual interest. Specific teaching responsibilities will include teaching basic statistics and other aspects of social and administrative pharmacy, such as quality measurement, to pharmacy students, and data management (including use and applications of statistical software and artificial intelligence) to graduate students. Areas of research interest may include pharmaceutical marketing, pharmacy management, practice research, pharmacoeconomics, pharmacoepidemiology, outcomes research, health policy, or social behavioral research. The successful applicant will have opportunities to collaborate with eight full-time pharmacy administration faculty and to capitalize on collaborative relationships with faculty in other academic departments on campus. The successful applicant will also enjoy affiliation with the Research Institute of Pharmaceutical Sciences and collaborative opportunities with the Center for Pharmaceutical Marketing and Management, a center of excellence in pharmaceutical marketing, pharmacy management, and medication use outcomes research, and is home to Medicare, Medicaid and other data that support its research mission. The position offers the potential for growth in an established program committed to excellence in pharmacy and graduate education.  The University of Mississippi is the flagship university for the State of Mississippi. A world-class public research university, the institution has a long history of producing leaders in public service, academics and innovative research. The School of Pharmacy is on the main campus in Oxford, a community of approximately 19,000 residents that has been recognized nationally as one of America’s best places to live. The Chronicle of Higher Education has named The University of Mississippi as one of the “Great Colleges to Work For.” The position is available beginning July 1, 2026, but a later start date is acceptable. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or until an adequate applicant pool is established. The search will continue until a suitable candidate is selected. Interested applicants should submit an application, letter of intent outlining his/her qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, teaching and research statements, and the names and contact information of at least three references through The University of Mississippi’s online employment site at https://olemiss.edu/hr/um-careers/. For additional information please contact, Erin Holmes, PhD, Search Committee Chair, 662-915-5914, erholmes@olemiss.edu.  The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity for qualified individuals in employment and education programs and activities. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee, student, or applicant. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Responsibilities for this position include: teaching at the professional and graduate levels, initiation of research projects, and participation in collaborative research projects of mutual interest. Specific teaching responsibilities will include teaching basic statistics and other aspects of social and administrative pharmacy, such as quality measurement, to pharmacy students, and data management (including use and applications of statistical software and artificial intelligence) to graduate students. Areas of research interest may include pharmaceutical marketing, pharmacy management, practice research, pharmacoeconomics, pharmacoepidemiology, outcomes research, health policy, or social behavioral research. Education Qualifications: PhD (Required) Experience: Relevant experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Dr-Melody---Gov-Ronnie-Musgrove-Endowed-Chair-of-Special-Education_JR101870": {
      "title": "Dr. Melody & Gov. Ronnie Musgrove Endowed Chair of Special Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-10\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Teacher Education Job Summary: Performs the functions of teaching, research or creative activities, and service and are assigned to an academic unit appropriate for their Discipline descriptor. The University of Mississippi invites applications for the inaugural Ronnie and Melody Musgrove Endowed Chair in Special Education. This prestigious position honors former Mississippi Governor Ronnie Musgrove, a lifelong advocate for education, and his late wife, Dr. Melody Musgrove, a former faculty member in the School of Education who held numerous leadership roles in education at the state and national levels. Job Description: Tenure Track Faculty members perform the functions of teaching, research or creative activities, and service and are assigned to an academic unit appropriate for their Discipline descriptor. Tenure Track Faculty members are usually hired as assistant professors and enter the tenure track. For example, an assistant professor must serve a probationary period of five years and be reviewed for tenure during his or her sixth year of continuous employment at the University. Tenure Track Faculty members may be hired, particularly at the associate and full ranks, with a reduction in the tenure probationary period, as explained in the Tenure Policy. Tenure Track Faculty members at the Associate and Full ranks are full members of the Graduate Faculty, while those at the Assistant rank are Associate Members of the Graduate Faculty. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Qualifications: - Earned doctorate and substantial experience in the field of special education.  - Minimum of five years of professional experience in special education, with demonstrated impact in academic, policy, or leadership roles - Proven ability to lead initiatives that result in meaningful and lasting contributions to the field - Strong record of scholarship, teaching, or policy work relevant to special education Preferred Qualifications: K-12 and post-secondary teaching experience preferred. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit the following: - A cover letter outlining your qualifications and vision for the role - A current curriculum vitae - A completed online application Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Education Qualifications: PhD: Special Education (Required) Experience: Relevant experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Chair-of-Theatre---Film_JR103478": {
      "title": "Chair of Theatre & Film",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nDepartment: The Department of Theatre & Film Job Summary: The Department of Theatre & Film at the University of Mississippi seeks a collaborative, visionary, and experienced academic leader to serve as Chair. This is a tenured, full-time, 12-month administrative faculty appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor (preference for Professor), reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts. The Chair provides academic, artistic, and administrative leadership for the department’s faculty, staff, and students; teaches one course per semester; and remains active as a scholar or creative artist. Job Description: The Department of Theatre & Film at the University of Mississippi (UM) invites applications for the position of Chair, to begin July 1, 2027. The appointment carries tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with a preference for the rank of Professor. The initial Chair appointment is renewable following quadrennial review. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience and includes an administrative stipend. We seek a leader who can bring faculty, staff, and students together around a shared vision for the department's future. The next Chair will build trust and collegiality, lead through open communication and transparent decision-making, and support shared governance. Candidates will be asked to articulate a compelling vision for the future and growth of the department, one that includes collaboration within the department and across departments, centers, and units on campus, and that is informed by University, College, and Departmental Strategic Plans. The department offers undergraduate degrees in theatre and film to more than 120 majors, including the BA in Theatre Arts, the BFA in Film Production, and the BFA in Theatre Arts with emphases in Design & Theatre Production and in Acting for Stage & Screen. Students have access to three theatrical venues, two soundstages, and various informal production spaces on campus and in the surrounding community. The University of Mississippi is a National Association of Schools of Theatre accredited institution. Candidates are welcome from any discipline of theatre, film, or related fields. The successful candidate will have: A track record and experience commensurate with appointment as Associate or Full Professor with tenure within the College of Liberal Arts (preference for Full Professor); A current or prior tenure appointment from an accredited University; Demonstrated outstanding accomplishments in teaching, research and/or creative achievement, and service and administration; Demonstrated leadership skills, including outstanding personnel management and interpersonal skills, and ideally experience with fiscal management; A strong commitment to undergraduate education, knowledge of broad curricular and academic issues in the field, and an understanding of areas of growth and interest in theatre and film that may attract students to the discipline; A commitment to the professional development of faculty, staff, and students; and A demonstrated commitment to the continued development of the Department of Theatre & Film, including a strong vision for collaboration within the department and across campus. Applications should be submitted online via the Faculty Career Site portal, accessible from https://olemiss.edu/hr/um-careers/ by clicking through to External Applicants > Faculty Openings. A complete application comprises (1) a cover letter addressing the candidate’s leadership and administrative experience, research and/or creative achievements, and preparation for this role; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a leadership statement detailing the candidate’s approach to leading a collaborative academic unit; and (4) the names, titles, and contact information of five professional references. Review of applications will begin January 11, 2027, and all applications received by that date will receive priority consideration. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Questions should be sent to theatrefilmsearch@olemiss.edu. ––– Founded in 1848, the University of Mississippi (UM), affectionately known to alumni, students and friends as Ole Miss, is Mississippi’s flagship university. Included in the elite group of “R1: Very High Research Spending and Doctorate Production” institutions by the Carnegie Classification, it has a long history of producing leaders in public service, academics, and business. The University of Mississippi is consistently named by The Chronicle of Higher Education as a “Great College to Work For,” and with a student body of approximately 28,000 students, it is the state’s largest university and is ranked among the nation’s fastest-growing institutions. Oxford, MS, is a vibrant university town and a recognized literary and arts destination, about an hour south of Memphis, TN. Each year the community hosts the Oxford Film Festival, the Double Decker Arts Festival, and the Oxford Blues Festival, among other gatherings. UM sponsors the Oxford Conference for the Book and a yearlong performing arts series at the Gertrude C. Ford Center for the Performing Arts and offers rich collaborative opportunities through the College of Liberal Arts’ Institute for the Arts, the University Museum, and the Yoknapatawpha Arts Council. Oxford is also known for its music scene, exceptional culinary offerings, historic landmarks, and the home of Nobel Prize-winning author William Faulkner. The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, ethnicity, age, disability, military status, protected veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Provide academic, artistic, and administrative leadership for the department, working collaboratively with faculty and staff to develop and advance a shared vision and strategic plan aligned with the goals of the College of Liberal Arts and the University Strategic Plan. Foster a collegial, transparent, and respectful departmental culture; support shared governance; communicate openly with faculty, staff, and students; and address concerns and disagreements constructively and fairly. Direct faculty and staff hiring, annual reviews, mentoring, workload and service assignments, and reappointment, tenure, and promotion processes, and support the professional development of faculty, staff, and students. Oversee curriculum development, course planning and scheduling, and assessment for the department’s undergraduate degree programs, and identify and develop areas of growth that attract and retain students. Administer the department’s budget, facilities, and equipment, including its theatrical venues, soundstages, and production spaces, and manage resources responsibly and transparently. Oversee the department’s theatre seasons and film productions in collaboration with faculty and staff. Build partnerships within the department, across campus, and with alumni, donors, and community and professional partners to enhance opportunities for students and faculty. Teach one course per semester and maintain an active program of research and/or creative activity. Represent the department within the College and University, serve on departmental, College, and University committees, and perform other duties as assigned by the Dean. Education Qualifications: PhD (Required) Experience: Relevant experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Research-Assistant-Professor---Mississippi-Mineral-Resources-Institute--MMRI--and-Center-for-Marine-Resources-and-Environmental-Technology--CMRET-_JR103475": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor - Mississippi Mineral Resources Institute (MMRI) and Center for Marine Resources and Environmental Technology (CMRET)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Mississippi Mineral Resources Institute Job Summary: Performs a limited range of duties with a principal assignment(s) for conducting research. Not eligible for tenure. Job Description: The Mississippi Mineral Resources Institute (MMRI) and the Center for Marine Resources and Environmental Technology (CMRET) at the University of Mississippi invite applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant Research Professor specializing in Computational Geosciences, beginning in January 2027. This is a full-time, 12-month, grant-funded research appointment initially offered for one year, with the possibility of extension for up to two additional years, subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance.   The ideal candidate will have a strong background in mathematics, computational methods, scientific programming, and advanced data analytics, with demonstrated experience applying AI and ML techniques to geoscientific problems. Areas of particular interest include remote sensing, bathymetric and topographic data analysis, acoustic imaging, geophysical data processing, and the characterization and imaging of Earth's surface and subsurface environments, including marine settings. The successful candidate is expected to develop and contribute to an active research program involving computational geosciences, advanced data analysis, and the development of innovative AI/ML methodologies for interpreting complex geospatial and geophysical datasets. The candidate will actively participate in research, student mentoring, and service activities within MMRI-CMRET, which operates within the University of Mississippi School of Engineering. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration with the School's nine academic departments, as well as national and international research partners. Applicants should demonstrate substantial expertise in computational sciences, mathematics, acoustics, data analytics, scientific programming, and/or geosciences, supported by peer-reviewed publications, externally funded research, or other significant scholarly accomplishments. Experience mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in independent research and a demonstrated ability to work effectively within interdisciplinary and collaborative research teams are highly desirable. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Essential Duties and Responsibilities Conduct original research involving artificial intelligence, machine learning, and computational methods applied to geoscientific problems. Develop, implement, and validate advanced computational algorithms for processing, analyzing, and interpreting geophysical, acoustic, bathymetric, topographic, and remote sensing datasets. Contribute to the preparation of research proposals and the pursuit of external funding from federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Publish research findings in peer-reviewed scientific journals and present results at national and international conferences. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students engaged in computational geoscience and related research activities. Collaborate with MMRI-CMRET researchers, faculty across the School of Engineering, and external academic, government, and industry partners. Participate in institute research initiatives, project management, technical reporting, and other scholarly and service activities. Position Expectations This is an in-person position based at the University of Mississippi, main campus in Oxford (MS). The successful candidate is expected to maintain a regular on-campus presence and actively participate in the daily research and collaborative activities of MMRI-CMRET. The successful candidate must demonstrate professionalism, effective communication skills, and the ability to establish and maintain productive, collegial working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external research partners. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Mathematics, Electrical Engineering, Physics, Geophysics, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution of higher education, conferred by the date of appointment. Demonstrated experience in scientific computing, mathematical modeling, programming, data analytics, artificial intelligence, or machine learning. Evidence of an active research agenda, or demonstrated potential to establish a productive research program, in computational science and/or geosciences. Evidence of experience or demonstrated potential for effective mentoring of undergraduate or graduate students, particularly in computational and data-intensive research. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research experience or equivalent professional research experience in a university, research institute, national laboratory, or comparable research organization. Significant experience in seafloor imaging, marine geophysical mapping, bathymetric data analysis, and/or acoustic remote sensing. Advanced proficiency in developing and applying AI/ML algorithms to large, complex geospatial or geophysical datasets. Record of peer-reviewed scientific publications and participation in externally funded research projects related to computational geosciences. Evidence of effective collaboration within multidisciplinary research teams at the national or international level. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title). Education Qualifications: PhD (Required) Experience: Related Experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Instructional-Assistant-Professor---Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_JR103471": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Electrical and Computer Engineering Job Summary: Primarily performs a limited range of duties. And are usually assigned teaching or service roles. Not eligible for tenure. Job Description: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Mississippi invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position at the INSTRUCTIONAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR level, beginning in August 2027. Primary responsibilities will include instruction of undergraduate courses in the general area of computer engineering such as Digital Logic Design, Advanced Digital Systems, Computer Architecture, and Embedded Systems, with specific assignments based on the departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Additional duties may include instruction of graduate courses, advising student teams, participating in recruiting and orientation events, and other departmental service activities. This is a permanent, non-tenure track position with opportunities for promotion through the instructional faculty ranks. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities will include instruction of undergraduate courses in the general area of computer engineering such as Digital Logic Design, Advanced Digital Systems, Computer Architecture, and Embedded Systems, with specific assignments based on the departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Additional duties may include instruction of graduate courses, advising student teams, participating in recruiting and orientation events, and other departmental service activities. This is a permanent, non-tenure track position with opportunities for promotion through the instructional faculty ranks. Minimum Qualifications All candidates are required to have earned a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field at the time of appointmentbefore beginning this position. Competitive candidates will have demonstrable teaching ability, strong interpersonal and communication skills, and an energetic commitment to undergraduate education.   Application Procedures Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications must include a cover letter, a current CV, a statement on teaching experience and philosophy, and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Any questions regarding this position should be addressed to the Search Committee Chair (Prof. Mustafa Matalgah) via email at mustafa@olemiss.edu.   Education Qualifications: PhD (Required) Experience: Related Experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice_JR103472": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Mechanical Engineering Job Summary: Performs duties in instruction, including the teaching of practical skills and demonstrating best professional. Not eligible for tenure. Job Description: The University of Mississippi invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Practice in Product Realization in the Department of Mechanical Engineering. This position reflects the university’s growing emphasis on connecting design, materials, manufacturing  processes, and testing with real-world product realization, transforming concepts into products. The successful candidate will develop and deliver innovative undergraduate courses and labs that bridge the gap between design intent and manufacturability. Instruction will cover the principles and applications of fundamental and advanced fabricating methods, including machining, casting, molding, thermoforming, sheet metal forming, additive manufacturing, digital fabrication, prototyping, and process control.  Developed courses will be accessible to students within the School of Engineering. Preference will be given to candidates with significant industry experience in aerospace, automotive, energy, or related advanced manufacturing sectors. Candidates should demonstrate an ability to translate professional expertise into hands-on learning environments that prepare graduates for leadership roles in modern engineering firms. Candidates should also be familiar with industry applications of artificial intelligence and smart manufacturing, such as data-driven process monitoring and control, predictive maintenance, machine vision for quality inspection, and digital twins, and be able to bring these practices into the classroom and lab. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Key Responsibilities: Curriculum Development and Instruction: Develop and teach courses in Product Realization with an emphasis on modern and digitally enabled engineering design and fabrication technologies, including : Introduction to Product Realization : Design-for-manufacture, prototyping, material selection, tolerance and quality considerations, sustainability. Fundamentals of Manufacturing : core processes including machining, casting, molding, forming, joining, and additive manufacturing, taught through the lens of process selection, design, and cost/rate/quality trade-offs. Digital Fabrication and Automation : Industry 4.0 concepts, connected machines and sensors (IIoT), robotics and automation, and digital twins of products and processes. AI and Data-Driven Process Control : statistical process control and quality systems extended with machine learning for process monitoring, predictive maintenance, machine vision inspection, and data-driven decision-making on the factory floor. Experiential Learning and Mentorship: Develop and oversee hands-on labs and design-build projects that reinforce course concepts and emphasize iterative design, testing and validation, systems-level thinking, and data-driven decision-making. Mentor students in product realization pathways. Provide students with real-world project opportunities through industry-sponsored collaborations. Industry and Academic Collaboration: Build partnerships with regional and national companies to provide internships, co-ops, and collaborative projects. Incorporate guest lectures, case studies, and applied research opportunities with industry partners. Encourage interdisciplinary collaboration with the Center for Manufacturing Excellence and others. Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees in Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Industrial Engineering, or a closely related field are required. Industry Experience: A minimum of five years of professional experience in the aerospace, automotive, or related manufacturing industries with a focus on manufacturing processes and process control is required. Teaching and Mentoring: Proven experience in teaching or mentoring in academic or professional settings. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with a multidisciplinary engineering student body. Preferred Qualifications: Experience collaborating with engineering design and product development programs. Familiarity with interdisciplinary teaching approaches integrating engineering and business practices. Industry experience applying artificial intelligence, machine learning, or advanced production technologies (e.g., Industry 4.0, connected sensors and IIoT, automation, digital twins) to production environments. Education Qualifications: Master's (Required) Experience: Related Experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Assistant-Professor-of-Finance_JR103355": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Department of Finance Job Summary: The Department of Finance in the School of Business Administration at The University of Mississippi invites applications for a tenure-track position to start in August, 2027. Job Description: Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate is expected to teach undergraduate, MBA, and/or doctoral level courses in finance and to perform duties assigned by the Dean of the School of Business Administration and Chair of the Department of Finance. The normal teaching load for a research-active faculty member is 2/2 (6 credit hours each semester, Fall and Spring) with the option to teach summer courses for additional pay subject to course and funding availability. A strong record of quality research and teaching is required for tenure. Advanced assistant professor is preferred.   Required Qualifications: To be considered, applicants must have earned a doctorate degree in finance (or hold ABD status with expected degree completion prior to August, 2027) from an AACSB accredited or well-regarded business program. Candidates must have demonstrated research and teaching interests in finance. Candidates should possess a proven track record of original research and/or publication in quality finance journals, and must provide evidence of a strong commitment to scholarship, effective teaching, and service. No candidate will be considered who does not meet the departmental AACSB standards for Scholarly Academics (SA). Advanced assistant professor is preferred. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: The successful candidate is expected to teach undergraduate, MBA, and/or doctoral level courses in finance and to perform duties assigned by the Dean of the School of Business Administration and Chair of the Department of Finance. The normal teaching load for a research-active faculty member is 2/2 (6 credit hours each semester, Fall and Spring) with the option to teach summer courses for additional pay subject to course and funding availability. A strong record of quality research and teaching is required for tenure. Application Procedure: Screening of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled or until an adequate applicant pool is achieved. Apply online (only) at https://careers.olemiss.edu . Applications cannot be accepted in any other format. Candidates should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter, and evidence of effective teaching. At least three references will be required from candidates invited to campus. For additional information, contact the search committee chair, Dr. Robert Van Ness, 329 Holman Hall, School of Business Administration, PO Box 1848, The University of Mississippi, University, MS 38677-1848 (rvanness@olemiss.edu ). Education Qualifications: PhD: Finance (Required) Experience: Related Experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    },
    "https://olemiss.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/External__Faculty/job/University-MS/Assistant-Professor-of-Scenic-Design_JR103482": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nDepartment: The Department of Theatre & Film at The University of Mississippi currently enrolls approximately 120 majors and has 30 full-time faculty members. The department offers a BA in Theatre Arts and BFA programs in Acting for Stage & Screen and Design & Theatre Production, as well as a BFA in Film Production. The University of Mississippi, which has been recognized by The Chronicle of Higher Education for seventeen consecutive years as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, is located in Oxford, MS, and frequently ranked as one of the “Best College Towns in the Nation” by multiple sources. Founded in 1848, the University of Mississippi is Mississippi's flagship university. Included in the elite group of R-1: Doctoral Universities - Highest Research Activity by the Carnegie Classification, it has a long history of producing leaders in public service, academics and business. With more than 24,000 students, The University of Mississippi is the state's largest university and is ranked among the nation's fastest-growing institutions. Its 15 academic divisions include a major medical school, nationally recognized schools of accountancy, law and pharmacy, and the Sally McDonnell Barksdale Honors College, renowned for a blend of academic rigor, experiential learning and opportunities for community action. Join the Ole Miss Family - Build Your Legacy Here! Job Summary: The Department of Theatre & Film at The University of Mississippi invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design beginning August 2027. Job Description: This full-time, tenure-track, nine-month position focuses on scenic design for the Department of Theatre & Film. The successful candidate should demonstrate a commitment to teaching, professional creative practice, and collaborative work in an academic production environment. Responsibilities include supervising and executing scenic designs in collaboration with other faculty, staff, and student designers each semester at a Research I University; teaching undergraduate scenic design courses at both the lower and upper division; maintaining and growing a strong record of professional creative work outside the department; and performing service appropriate to the position including recruitment and participation in shared governance. Additional responsibilities will include designing and oversight of scenic design within the department’s mainstage season, property construction, and other areas of production, and mentoring students in their academic and artistic development, technical skills, and career preparation. Applicants should complete the University’s online application form at https://careers.olemiss.edu/ and submit a letter of intent, a Curriculum Vitae, link to an online portfolio or professional website, and list of references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will remain open until an adequate pool has been established. More information about the department can be found at theatreandfilm.olemiss.edu. Join the Ole Miss Family — Build Your Legacy Here! Job Responsibilities: Responsibilities include supervising and executing scenic designs in collaboration with other faculty, staff, and student designers each semester at a Research I University; teaching undergraduate scenic design courses at both the lower and upper division; maintaining and growing a strong record of professional creative work outside the department; and performing service appropriate to the position including recruitment and participation in shared governance. Additional responsibilities will include designing and oversight of scenic design within the department’s mainstage season, property construction, and other areas of production, and mentoring students in their academic and artistic development, technical skills, and career preparation. Education Qualifications: PhD Experience: Related Experience Interview Requirement: Interview Requirements: Any candidate who is called for an interview must notify the Department of Equal Opportunity/Regulatory Compliance in writing of any reasonable accommodation needed prior to the date of the interview. EEO Statement: The University of Mississippi provides equal opportunity in any employment practice, education program, or education activity to all qualified persons. The University complies with all applicable laws regarding equal opportunity and affirmative action and does not unlawfully discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based upon race, color, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, citizenship, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or genetic information. Background Check Statement: The University of Mississippi is committed to providing a safe campus community. UM conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check."
    }
